  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 845736,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "'99 Kōshien is a high school baseball simulation game for the Sony PlayStation, part of the popular Kōshien series released in Japan. Based on real-life athletes, the game allows players to experience the thrill of the Kōshien tournament, Japan's prestigious national high school baseball championship. \n\nPlayers manage and control a team of high school baseball players, strategizing through batting orders, pitching rotations, and fielding formations. The gameplay focuses on realistic baseball mechanics, requiring players to master timing, pitch selection, and defensive positioning. \n\nBeyond the core baseball simulation, '99 Kōshien likely features a robust team management system, allowing players to develop their players' skills and build a championship-caliber squad. The game aims to capture the intensity and drama of the Kōshien tournament, offering a compelling experience for fans of baseball and sports simulation games. It continues the series' tradition of bringing the excitement of Japanese high school baseball to the PlayStation."
    },
